Task prompt: The `TaskReport` class currently handles processing raw data, formatting it, and displaying the final report. Your task is to refactor this class into three separate classes, each with a single responsibility, to improve modularity and adhere to the Single Responsibility Principle.

Current code in the editor:
```
class TaskReport {
    constructor(tasks) {
        this.tasks = tasks;
    }

    generateReport() {
        // TODO: This method violates SRP. It handles data processing, formatting, and display.
        // Create separate classes for each responsibility:
        // 1. Data processing (e.g., TaskDataProcessor)
        // 2. Report rendering/formatting (e.g., ReportRenderer)
        // 3. Report exporting/displaying (e.g., ReportExporter)

        const processedData = this.tasks.map(task => ({
            name: task.name,
            status: task.completed ? "Completed" : "Pending",
            duration: task.durationHours // Assume duration in hours
        }));

        let reportString = "# Task Status Report\n\n";
        processedData.forEach(item => {
            reportString += `- **${item.name}**: ${item.status} (${item.duration} hours)\n`;
        });

        console.log(reportString); // This is a display responsibility
        return reportString;
    }
}

// Example usage (will need adjustment after refactoring)
const myTasks = [
    { name: "Design Database", completed: true, durationHours: 8 },
    { name: "Implement API", completed: false, durationHours: 20 },
    { name: "Write Tests", completed: false, durationHours: 10 }
];

